Aria (Presales): Need a compact POC handoff for AcmeCorp tomorrow morning. They want: streaming SDK quickstart (Node + Go), an example of a function/tool-call that enforces a response schema, webhook signing example, handshake cURL for ephemeral tokens, short security answers (KMS, retention, SOC2 link), and two pricing options (reserved + burst vs pay-as-you-go placeholders). Can we get a one-screen cheat and callouts for common enterprise blockers?

Noah (Platform Eng): Ill draft. A few specifics Ill include: signed webhooks (X-RW-Signature header), schema hash validation on the client (schemaHash), short-lived STS token flow for ephemeral creds, and a fallback routing rule to a quantized variant. Also will call out Dedicated provisioning lead time and SAML gaps.

Cal (Sales): Perfect. They insisted logs remain non-persistent unless customer opts-in. Legal also wants a note on export controls & DPA pointer. Finance will fill the $ placeholders.

Aria (Presales): Yes to non-persistent logs default. Add a tiny troubleshooting table: 401 ephemeral token issues, webhook signature mismatch, SSE disconnects (CORS/Accept header). Keep it terse.

Noah (Platform Eng): Draft cheat (compact bullets + snippets):
- Objective: Demo streaming chat + function/tool call with schema enforcement and signed webhook delivery.
- Env: Hosted (eu), primary model r-infer-2, fallback r-infer-2-quant-sm.
- Auth: short-lived STS token example (exchange server -> /v1/token); KMS for long-term keys; TLS required.

Node (stream + schema-enforced function call + signed webhook):
```js
// Node example (minimal)
const client = new Redwood({ token: process.env.RW_TOKEN, region: 'eu' });
const s = client.chat.stream({ model: 'r-infer-2' });
s.on('delta', e => {
  if (e.kind === 'function_call' && e.schemaHash === 'sha256:abc123') {
    // enforce schema before calling tool
    const payload = JSON.parse(e.payload);
    // call signed webhook
    fetch('https://hooks.acme/exec', {
      method: 'POST',
      headers: { 'Content-Type': 'application/json', 'X-RW-Signature': sign(payload) },
      body: JSON.stringify(payload)
    });
  }
});
```

Go (stream receive + validate schemaHash):
```go
// Go pseudo
cli := redwood.NewClient(os.Getenv("RW_TOKEN"))
stream := cli.ChatStream(ctx, redwood.ChatParams{Model:"r-infer-2", Region:"eu"})
for ev := range stream.Events() {
  if ev.Type == redwood.EventFunctionCall && ev.SchemaHash == "sha256:abc123" {
    // validate then post
    http.Post("https://hooks.acme/exec", "application/json", bytes.NewReader(ev.Payload))
  }
}
```

Handshake cURL (ephemeral token exchange + SSE connect):
1) exchange: `curl -X POST https://auth.redwood.ai/v1/token -d 'client_id=acme&grant_type=urn:aws:sts'` -> returns short-lived token
2) connect: `curl -H "Authorization: Bearer $RW_TOKEN" -H "Accept: text/event-stream" "https://api.redwood.ai/v1/streams/chat?model=r-infer-2&region=eu"`

Operational knobs and fallback: set batching window 10-20ms, enable KV prefix cache, enable model quantization for fallback. Route to r-infer-2-quant-sm when queued requests > 75% or 99p latency > 120ms.

Security quick answers:
- Data residency: EU-only endpoints for this POC; Private (VPC) available for Dedicated.
- Encryption: TLS in transit; KMS-managed keys at rest; HSM optional.
- Logs: inference logs non-persistent by default; can enable with customer consent and configurable retention.
- Compliance: SOC2 attestation link will be added by Legal; DPA available.
- Incident response: IR contact secops@redwood.ai; standard timeline & post-incident report offered.

Pricing (placeholders):
- Option A: Reserved capacity + burst bucket (best unit cost) -> estimate: $<FINANCE_FILL>/day for baseline 2k QPS + burst buffer.
- Option B: Pay-as-you-go hosted (pilot) -> estimate: $<FINANCE_FILL>/day.

Enterprise blockers & notes:
- Dedicated capacity provisioning: typical lead time 2-4 weeks for GPU reservations.
- SSO/SAML: Onprem/Private needs additional config; SAML connectors available but legal review may add time.
- KMS integration: show required KMS API access & rotation policy.
- Export controls: flagged for legal review if model weights cross jurisdictions.

Troubleshooting quick hits:
- 401 on connect: check STS exchange, token TTL, and system clock skew.
- Webhook 403 / signature mismatch: verify webhook secret and signature algorithm (HMAC-SHA256).
- SSE stalls/disconnects: ensure `Accept: text/event-stream`, CORS allowed, and no proxy injecting content.

